     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. At 50 mg, the patient could develop severe low blood pressure, a fast heart rate and shock. Calcium channel blocker overdose is hard to reverse, and amlodipine's long half-life (30\u201350 hours) makes it last longer.\n\nThis may be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose. Which do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **A different dose within 2.5\u201310 mg**\n3. **50 mg as written.** If this is really intended, please confirm and tell me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note. Your institution's order system or pharmacy may still require a separate review.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
